<h2>Quick reference: what to look for</h2>
<div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Roof or component</th><th>Hail signs</th><th>Often confused with</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>Asphalt three-tab and architectural</td><td>Soft bruises, dark circular granule loss, fractured tabs and ridge caps</td><td>Blistering, thermal cracking, foot scuffs, uniform aging</td></tr>
<tr><td>Standing seam metal</td><td>Dents on panels and seams, cracked paint at dents, seam deformation</td><td>Oil canning (waviness from installation or expansion)</td></tr>
<tr><td>R-panel metal</td><td>Dents, crushed ribs, damaged fastener washers, coating loss</td><td>Loose fasteners from thermal movement, rust from age</td></tr>
<tr><td>Clay tile</td><td>Cracks from impact points, broken corners and edges</td><td>Foot-traffic cracks across bearing points</td></tr>
<tr><td>Concrete tile</td><td>Spalling, chipped edges, coating popped off at impacts, cracks</td><td>Surface erosion and efflorescence from age</td></tr>
<tr><td>Flat and low-slope</td><td>Punctures, membrane fractures, crushed insulation, bruised mod bit</td><td>Shrinkage, seam failure from age, ponding wear</td></tr>
<tr><td>Wood shake</td><td>Fresh splits with light wood inside and sharp edges, impact marks</td><td>Weathered drying splits, gray inside</td></tr>
<tr><td>Soft metals</td><td>Round dents, spatter marks, flattened condenser fins</td><td>Ladder dents, older dents from previous storms</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div>

<h2>What to do with what you find</h2>
<p>Once you have photos of likely hail damage, pin down the storm date with our <a href="/tools/storm-report-lookup/">storm report lookup</a> and report the claim. Then expect the insurer to look at the same signs described here, using test squares and soft metals. Our article on <a href="/post/how-insurance-companies-evaluate-hail-damage/">how insurance companies evaluate hail damage</a> explains their process, and the <a href="/post/hail-damage-insurance-claim/">hail damage claim guide</a> covers everything from filing to final payment.</p>
<p>If the carrier's inspection missed damage you can see in your photos, our <a href="/services/roof-hail-damage-claims/">roof and hail damage claims</a> service starts with our own roof-level inspection and a full Xactimate estimate.</p>
